Patch 6011 (ENHANCEMENT): a port's keybinds profile, for a runtime that serves several games with different controls
(keybinds per game; the Ratchet & Clank collection is one runtime with one exe and one settings folder
per game, port/rc/rc_settings.{h,cpp}).
Builds on Project Helghast's keybinds.ini (the Killzone 3 PC port, same author, MIT: patches 2037, 2061, 4011, 4013,
4023, 4028 carried here as they are), and on its mouse settings (2069/2099/2101).
libs/input/pad_kb_profile.h (new, pure types, C and C++): PadKbProfile = the file's title, a default key table
(PadKbDefKey {input, key, key}), the uses the file's comments name (PadKbUse) and the defaults of a [mouse] section
(PadKbMouse: look on/off, sensitivity, zoom_sensitivity, invert_y; -1 / <= 0 = not set).
libs/input/pad_keybinds.h: pad_kb_profile (NULL = the built-in table and file, byte for byte as before: Project
Helghast's host test test_pad_keybinds.c passes unchanged and the default file is identical); with a profile,
pad_kb_defaults uses its table, the parser reads [mouse] (unknown keys and values logged, never fatal), the writer
names the profile's title and uses and writes [mouse]. PadKeybinds gains `mouse` at its end (zero without a profile).
libs/input/cellPad.c: cellPad_keybinds_profile(p) before the first read (later calls are logged and ignored);
cellPad_keybinds_mouse(out) reads the file now if needed (written with the profile's defaults when missing) and
returns its [mouse] section, so the port can feed the mouse switches (KZ3_MOUSE_*) before the window opens.
The file's place is unchanged here: the port names it with KZ3_KEYBINDS (port/rc/rc_settings.cpp: the per-game folder).
Host test: port/rc/tests/run_rc_settings_test.sh.

